---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { allTopics } from '../../lib/data';
const groups = [
  ['Module 1: Development of practical skills (AS and A level, all papers)', 'Module 1'],
  ['Module 2: Foundations in chemistry (AS and A level, all papers)', 'Module 2'],
  ['Module 3: Periodic table and energy (AS and A level; A-level Papers 1 and 3)', 'Module 3'],
  ['Module 4: Core organic chemistry (AS and A level; A-level Papers 2 and 3)', 'Module 4'],
  ['Module 5: Physical chemistry and transition elements (A level only; Papers 1 and 3)', 'Module 5'],
  ['Module 6: Organic chemistry and analysis (A level only; Papers 2 and 3)', 'Module 6'],
];
---
<Base title="OCR A-level Chemistry questions by topic (every paper since 2016)" description="Every OCR Chemistry A past-paper question since 2016 sorted into 40 topics across the six modules, each with mark schemes and examiners' comments." context="questions-index">
  <h1>Questions by topic</h1>
  <p>Every OCR AS and A-level Chemistry A past-paper question since June 2016, sorted into the topics of the six modules. Each topic page shows every question with its mark scheme and the examiner's comment, with filters by paper, year and question type. Paper 3 (Unified chemistry) questions appear under whichever topic they assess.</p>
  {groups.map(([h, key]) => (
    <>
      <h2 class="strand-head">{h}</h2>
      <ul class="topic-list">
        {allTopics.filter((t) => t.paper === key).map((t) => <li><a href={`/questions/${t.slug}/`}><span>{t.name}</span><span class="strand"><span class={`badge badge-${t.paper.replace('Module ', '')}`}>{t.paper.replace('Module ', 'M')}</span> {t.parts} parts</span></a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </>
  ))}
  <h2>By question type</h2>
  <p>Or work on a kind of question across every topic: <a href="/questions/type/multiple-choice/">multiple choice</a>, <a href="/questions/type/calculations/">calculations</a>, <a href="/questions/type/equations/">equations</a>, <a href="/questions/type/mechanisms/">mechanisms</a>, <a href="/questions/type/structures-and-isomers/">structures and isomers</a>, <a href="/questions/type/six-mark-questions/">six-mark level of response</a>, <a href="/questions/type/practical-questions/">practical questions</a>, <a href="/questions/type/short-answer/">short answers</a>.</p>
</Base>
